            <Main applyHouseholdOperatingConditions="false" applyReducedOperatingConditions="false" atypicalElectricalLoads="true" waterConservation="true" referenceHouse="false">
                <Vermiculite code="3">
                    <English>No Vermiculite</English>
                    <French>Pas de Vermiculite</French>
                </Vermiculite>
            </Main>
            <AtypicalElectricalLoads deIcingCables="false" exteriorLighting="false" hotTub="true" heatedGarage="true" portableAirConditioning="false" pool="false" mixedUse="false" totalUnits="0" energyStarUnits="0" evChargingStation="false" outdoorGasAppliances="false" commonSpace="false" elevator="false" fitnessRoom="false" snowmeltSystem="false" unheatedGarage="false" />
            <WaterConservation LowFlushToilets="0" LowFlushToiletsUpgrade="3" />
            <RURComments xml:space="preserve">
                <airSeal>The infiltration test demonstrate air leakage on the following house components:

-Windows: We noticed some air leakage on some windows especially on the units located in the basement.

-Door: We noticed air leakage around the back door located in the living. The addition of weather stripping might reduce the leakage and increase the air tightness of the door.

-Receptacles: At the moment of the infiltration test, we noticed leakage from the receptacles. We recommend the installation of insulation custom made for electrical boxes.

-Mechanical equipment chimneys: We noticed air leakage from the furnace chimney. This situation is normal.

Overall, the infiltration test result showed that the house has a fairly good air tightness.  

</airSeal>
                <ceilings>At the time of the inspection we observed that the roof insulation level is R-30. We recommend adding insulation to meet the actual standard based at R-60.</ceilings>
                <windows>At the moment of the inspection the windows in place are Double panes with metal spacer. We recommend the replacement of all windows by ENERGY STAR CERTIFIED units suitable for northern climate and ZONE 3.</windows>
                <doors>We notices air leakage from the back door located in the living room on main floor. The exterior light was visible around the door. The addition of weather strips might help to reduce the gap between the door and the frame. If replacement of the unit, we recommend the use of an ENERGY STAR CERTIFIED product.</doors>
                <VentilationSystem>Following the infiltration test, the natural ventilation in the house is not enough. The house showed signs of a high level of humidity. We recommend the replacement of the air exchanger by an HRV (Heat Recovery Ventilator) unit, ENERGY STAR and HVI (Home Ventilation Institute) certified.</VentilationSystem>
                <WaterConservation>At the time of the inspection we noticed 3 13L toilets. We recommend the replacement by low flush toilet. This change might help to reduce your water cunsumption.</WaterConservation>
            </RURComments>
        </Options>
